# Availability Manifest SSOT

When working on ManifestWriter, availability index, data status, shard dimensions, or missing data:

**Read first:** `unified-trading-pm/codex/02-data/availability-manifest-and-data-status.md`

This document defines:
- Schema v4 (16 columns: date, venue, chain, data_type, instrument_type, league_id, timeframe, feature_group, model_family, training_period, strategy_id, client_id, instruction_type, instrument_count, service_name, written_at, schema_version)
- Per-service shard dimension matrix (L1-L8)
- Data status page tree hierarchy per service × category
- Availability % calculation (expected from UAC, found from manifest)
- Integrity principles (atomic shard failure, schema validation, UAC SSOT)
- DeFi chain grouping (venue=protocol, chain=chain, not venue=PROTOCOL-CHAIN)
- Sports bookmaker venues (PINNACLE, BETFAIR_EX, etc., not "ODDS_API")

**Never overload `venue`** with non-venue data. Use the proper column (feature_group, model_family, client_id, etc.).
